+\section{Two Controlled Case Studies}\label{sec:controlled-placement}
+The two studies test distinct observers. The transport observer sees TLS application-record lengths on a selected link. The tool-dispatch observer sees ordered tool names, write counts and response byte lengths, including failed calls; it is an instrumented dispatch view, not an encrypted-network observer. Neither experiment combines these views or runs an autonomous agent. Saved outputs and reference programs let us vary the specific boundary while holding the prescribed workload fixed.
 
-\subsection{Check 1 \& Check 3 on real TLS~1.2 streams: natural task-granularity gradient}
-For each of 24 public topics (12 training, 12 disjoint test topic clusters), \texttt{gpt-6-luna} generates a 1-sentence brief explanation ($105$--$160$ UTF-8 bytes) and a 6--8 sentence expanded explanation ($812$--$1{,}249$ bytes; 48 saved outputs). An upstream origin transmits each response over a real loopback TLS~1.2 connection (\texttt{ECDHE-RSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256}) to a frontend that decrypts, strips upstream padding and re-emits chunks over a second terminal TLS~1.2 connection captured by a transparent TCP relay. Every trial verifies exact plaintext SHA-256 recovery and parses actual TLS record type~23 application frames.
+\subsection{Transport placement and workload-matched framing}
